{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nThe sea at Scheveningen is a flat, grey nothing. I walked an hour through the woods to see it and found only damp sand and the smell of fish. A waste of boots, truly. The picture gallery here is decent, though the light in the afternoon was poor. I paid two guilders for a decent dinner in Delft earlier, which was reasonable.\n\nI sat in the Bois for an hour, watching the Dutch look at me with that peculiar, polite indifference. They are a people of water and trade, lacking that fiery spirit of the South, but they have their order. In the evening, three French comedies. The first was tiresome, the second decent, the third a farce of the lowest kind. I laughed, but mostly from relief that it was over.\n\nKarl writes that his Latin is improving. I hope his discipline holds. Do not worry about the cold; I have brought my best coat. I shall return to Berlin soon.\n\nYour loving,\nG.W.F. Hegel"}}],"created":1795218955,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":218,"prompt_tokens":1129,"total_tokens":1347,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-NGkgulnUre8ExHGdIne3WZODX5cELPpC","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":1129,"prompt_ms":1079.008,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.9557201062887511,"prompt_per_second":1046.3314451792758,"predicted_n":218,"predicted_ms":5115.867,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.57542396313364,"predicted_per_second":42.417052671619494}}